{
  "id": "scaffolding",
  "term": "scaffolding",
  "definition": "Scaffolding is support provided by a teacher or other more capable person that is adjusted to the learner’s needs so the learner can do more than they could independently. In sociocultural learning, this support can include not only explanations or questions but also cues such as tone of voice, facial expression, gaze, and gesture that direct attention and help build meaning.",
